@startuml rendering-pipeline-flowchart-gpu-backbuffer
title Gondwana - Desktop GPU RenderFrameSnapshot Mailbox
' Desktop-only: browser GPU does NOT use the snapshot mailbox.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FFF1D8
  BorderColor #B57521
  ArrowColor #B57521
}

|Engine thread|
start
repeat
  :Run simulation / background work;
  if (Foreground frame due?) then (yes)
    :Update surface effects and DirectDrawings;
    :TryBeginBuild() in 3-slot mailbox;
    if (Free slot available?) then (yes)
      :Resolve views, scene, layers,\nvisibility, animation and geometry;
      :Record immutable SKPicture commands\nwith RecordingBackbuffer;
      :Publish RenderFrameSnapshot;
      :Recycle previously published, unacquired frame;
    else (no)
      :Skip snapshot production this frame;
    endif
    :AfterFrameRender requests desktop GL repaint;
  endif
repeat while (Engine running?)
stop

|Desktop GL callback|
start
:Ensure GpuBackbuffer is initialized\nfor logical size, context and MSAA;
:TryAcquire newest published snapshot;
if (Snapshot available?) then (yes)
  if (Recorded dimensions match backbuffer?) then (yes)
    :BeginFrame;
    :Replay snapshot commands on GPU;
    :EndFrame (flush);
    :Snapshot GPU image;
  else (no)
    :Keep current GPU backbuffer\n(recording has stale logical size);
  endif
  :Release rendering slot;
else (no)
  :Reuse current GPU backbuffer;
endif
:Present image with aspect-preserving transform;
:Flush GL and RecordFrame;
stop

note right
  Mailbox ownership is protected by a short lock.
  Building, replay, and disposal happen outside it.
  A stalled renderer owns one slot while the producer
  can alternate the other two. The UI/window size
  does not change the logical backbuffer resolution.
end note
@enduml
